<HelpTab>
    <HelpSection Title="Positions">
        <FluentText>
            <a href="/manage/rota/positions">Positions</a> are the jobs people do, such as Marshal or Party Host.
            Each has a <strong>Name</strong>, a <strong>Description</strong> and a <strong>Colour on the rota</strong>.
            A position can also have:
        </FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Required training</strong>: courses staff must have completed before they can pick up its
                open shifts. Expand a position on the Positions page to set it. If you put someone without the
                training on a shift, the rota flags it.</li>
            <li>Contract requirements and time-off allowances that apply to everyone whose primary position it is.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Shift templates">
        <FluentText>
            <a href="/manage/rota/templates">Shift Templates</a> are the shifts a location needs every week and who they
            need, such as "Saturday AM, 09:00 to 14:00, 2 Duty Managers and 4 Hosts". Staff never see them.
        </FluentText>
        <ol>
            <li>Select <strong>New shift template</strong>.</li>
            <li>Give it a <strong>Name</strong>, pick the day under <strong>Every</strong>, and set when it
                <strong>Starts</strong> and <strong>Ends</strong>. An end time earlier than the start runs into the next day.</li>
            <li>Under <strong>Who it needs</strong>, choose a <strong>Position</strong> and <strong>How many</strong>.
                Use <strong>Add another position</strong> for each extra position.</li>
            <li>Optionally set <strong>Starting</strong> and <strong>Until</strong> dates, for example for school holidays only.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>
            Templates belong to one location; Admins pick the location at the top of the page. <strong>Archive</strong> a
            template you no longer need, and tick <strong>Show archived</strong> to find and <strong>Restore</strong> it.
            Archiving never changes shifts already on the rota.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Staff">
        <FluentText>
            Only people who hold a position appear on the rota. Give one person positions on the
            <strong>Rota</strong> tab of their profile under <a href="/manage/users">Users</a>. There you can also
            set their primary position, their own contract and allowances, their availability and their
            clock-in PIN.
        </FluentText>
        <FluentText>
            To change several people at once, use <a href="/manage/rota/staff">Staff</a>. Filter by location,
            position or name, tick people, then use <strong>Positions</strong>, <strong>Contract</strong> or
            <strong>Allowances</strong>.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Contract requirements">
        <FluentText>
            Minimum and maximum hours per week, minimum shifts per week and minimum shift length. Set a company
            default in Rota Settings, then override any single value for a position or a person. Leave a field
            blank to inherit it. The rota warns when someone's week doesn't meet their contract.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Rota settings">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Holiday year starts in</strong> and <strong>Day of the month</strong>: when allowances reset.</li>
            <li><strong>Hours in a working day</strong>: used to turn days of time off into hours.</li>
            <li><strong>Clock-in window (minutes)</strong>: how early before a shift staff can clock in.</li>
            <li><strong>Email staff a reminder before each shift</strong>, and how many hours before.</li>
            <li><strong>Payroll export</strong>: your pay period, and whether to take a break off long days in the export.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Clock-in terminals">
        <ol>
            <li>On the tablet that will stay at the venue, sign in and open <a href="/manage/rota/terminals">Clock-In Terminals</a>.</li>
            <li>Select <strong>Pair this device as a terminal</strong>, give it a name such as "Front desk tablet" and
                choose its location.</li>
            <li>Tick <strong>Sign me out on this device afterwards</strong> so staff can't use your account, then pair it.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>
            The tablet then shows today's staff, a PIN pad and a QR code that changes every 30 seconds.
            <strong>Unpair</strong> a terminal to stop it working straight away.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
